A||||20||Call||Question On T-Tops On Fieros||||5||
Z||000000||Call||12-27-1999||11:52 PM||||Hello, I am thinking about putting t-tops on the Fiero I am going to get and I have some questions, first, if the car doesn't come with T-Tops how much does it cost to have them put on? Also, when the T-Tops are on the car can you tell that they are there? Does anybody know a place on the internet where I can see some T-Tops on a Fiero when they are on and off? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-28-1999||03:15 AM||||The T-tops on a Fiero are smoked glass, not "solid" like on some of the older Vettes, so yes, you can see them when they're on the car.  I don't know what it would cost to have a set installed, but my guess is that it would be cheaper to buy a car with them already installed.  If you want some on your car and haven't done something like this before, may I suggest you pay the extra $$ and have them done professionally?  It wouldn't take much to get them out of alignment, IMHO. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttoparchive1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2FAST4U||12-28-1999||02:55 PM||||I just say a new (still in the box) T-Top set at auction on e-bay. bidding was already over $1,000.00. so I bet it won't be cheap. Good luck with th conversion. ||||reg||1
